  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING PROTECTION OF NORTHERN AND SOUTHERN WHITE-CHEEKED GIBBONS IN A SITE OF GLOBAL SIGNIFICANCE, THE NAM KADING NATIONAL PROTECTED AREA AND IMPROVING KNOWLEDGE OF THE CONSERVATION STATUS OF BOTH SPECIES IN BOLIKHAMXAY PROVINCE, LAO PDR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMMEDIATELY REDUCE THREATS TO EXISTING POPULATIONS OF NORTHERN AND SOUTHERN WHITE-CHEEKED GIBBONS IN LAOS, AND IMPLEMENT IMPROVED SPECIES MANAGEMENT STRATEGIES THROUGH COORDINATION, COMMUNITY ENGAGEMENT AND ADDRESSING INFORMATION GAPS. PROJECT OBJECTIVES INCLUDE THE FOLLOWING: (1) STRENGTHEN PROTECTION FOR WHITE-CHEEKED GIBBONS (N.LEUCOGENYS AND N. SIKI) AT BOTH NAM ET - PHOU LOUEY NATIONAL PARK (NEPL NP), AND NAM KADING NATIONAL PROTECTED AREA (NKD NPA) THROUGH INCREASED RANGER PATROLLING AND COORDINATED MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS (2) IMPROVE COOPERATION BETWEEN AGENCIES AND STAKEHOLDERS RESPONSIBLE FOR PROTECTING WHITE-CHEEKED GIBBONS (N.LEUCOGENYS) AND THEIR HABITAT AND ENSURE THAT PATROLLING EFFORTS SUPPORT COMMUNITY ENGAGEMENT ACTIVITIES THAT LINK SUPPORT WITH CONSERVATION AND (3) IMPROVE KNOWLEDGE OF CONSERVATION STATUS, DISTRIBUTION AND SITES OF SIGNIFICANCE FOR THE NORTHERN AND SOUTHERN WHITE-CHEEKED GIBBONS (N.LEUCOGENYS AND N. SIKI) IN NEPL NP AND NKD NPA.</narrative>
  </description>
